      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "1ff0f977decff85fbcef584598ddd97447274443",
            "subject": "LU-20983 quota: save LQA ranges for both MD and DT pools"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-29 23:03:40.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-10-29 23:03:40.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: run sanity-quota test_91 on the live fs",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: run sanity-quota test_91 on the live fs\n\ntest_91 reformatted and restarted the whole filesystem before and\nafter its check, so two formatall and a setupall dominated its run\ntime (385 s mean in CI, 94 s on a single node 1 MDT 2 OST VM).\n\nRun it on the mounted filesystem instead: enable user quota on the\nOSTs, create the pool, stop the MDS, delete the two OST index files\nand restart it, so the LU-17770 path with pool OSTs lacking an\nindex file at QMT start is still exercised. The pool, quota limit\nand quota_slave.enabled are restored on exit.\n\nEnabling only user quota is required: with ugp enabled the MDS\nhits an LBUG in qmt_seed_glbe_all() after the user index files are\nremoved.\n\nsanity-quota test_91, ldiskfs, 1 MDT 2 OST VM, 3 runs each:\n  before: 92, 99, 91 s\n  after:  61, 44, 45 s (44 s once warm)\n\nDepends on the ldiskfs-only skip in change 69759.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-quota env=ONLY=91\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I9d2659ec08aa8d82ba96a144fee363cde6b0400a\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
